:{"position":[[71,7]]}}}]],"pipeline":["stemmer"]}},{"documents":[],"index":{"version":"2.3.9","fields":["t"],"fieldVectors":[],"invertedIndex":[],"pipeline":["stemmer"]}},{"documents":[{"i":2,"t":"Document the public interface here. For each endpoint or function, list the purpose, parameters, response and errors.","s":"API overview","u":"/docs/api/overview","h":"","p":1},{"i":4,"t":"https://api.example.com/v1","s":"Base URL","u":"/docs/api/overview","h":"#base-url","p":1},{"i":6,"t":"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" https://api.example.com/v1/status","s":"Authentication","u":"/docs/api/overview","h":"#authentication","p":1},{"i":8,"t":"Field Type Description ok boolean true when the service is healthy version string Running version Response { \"ok\": true, \"version\": \"1.0.0\" }","s":"Example endpoint: GET /status","u":"/docs/api/overview","h":"#example-endpoint-get-status","p":1},{"i":10,"t":"Code Meaning 401 Missing or invalid token 429 Rate limit exceeded tip For larger APIs, generate this section from an OpenAPI file with the docusaurus-plugin-openapi-docs plugin instead of writing it by hand.","s":"Errors","u":"/docs/api/overview","h":"#errors","p":1},{"i":12,"t":"Describe the system at three levels: context (who and what it talks to), containers (the deployable parts) and components (the main modules inside each part).","s":"Architecture overview","u":"/docs/architecture/overview","h":"","p":11},{"i":15,"t":"Record significant decisions as short notes: the context, the decision, and the consequences. Link to the relevant issue or pull request. Decision Status Date Example: use a static site generator for docs Accepted 2026-10","s":"Design decisions","u":"/docs/architecture/overview","h":"#design-decisions","p":11},{"i":18,"t":"pnpm install pnpm start","s":"Local preview","u":"/docs/contributing/writing-docs","h":"#local-preview","p":16},{"i":20,"t":"docs/ holds the unreleased Next docs versioned_docs/ and versioned_sidebars/ hold frozen release snapshots (created by the command below) sidebars.ts controls navigation order","s":"Where things live","u":"/docs/contributing/writing-docs","h":"#where-things-live","p":16},{"i":22,"t":"pnpm run version:cut 1.0 This copies the current docs/ into versioned_docs/version-1.0. Commit the result alongside the release tag. The version dropdown updates automatically.","s":"Cutting a version at release time","u":"/docs/contributing/writing-docs","h":"#cutting-a-version-at-release-time","p":16},{"i":24,"t":"Sentence case headings One idea per page; link rather than repeat Every code block states its language; add a title when it is a file Use admonitions (:::tip, :::warning) sparingly","s":"Style","u":"/docs/contributing/writing-docs","h":"#style","p":16},{"i":27,"t":"Node.js 20 or later Git","s":"Requirements","u":"/docs/getting-started/installation","h":"#requirements","p":25},{"i":29,"t":"git clone https://github.com/rjmlaird/<project>.git cd <project> npm install","s":"Install","u":"/docs/getting-started/installation","h":"#install","p":25},{"i":31,"t":"npm test If the tests pass, continue to the quickstart.","s":"Verify","u":"/docs/getting-started/installation","h":"#verify","p":25},{"i":33,"t":"This page takes you from a fresh install to a working result in a few minutes.","s":"Quickstart","u":"/docs/getting-started/quickstart","h":"","p":32},{"i":35,"t":"config.yaml name: example log_level: info","s":"1. Create a config file","u":"/docs/getting-started/quickstart","h":"#1-create-a-config-file","p":32},{"i":37,"t":"npm start -- --config config.yaml","s":"2. Run the project","u":"/docs/getting-started/quickstart","h":"#2-run-the-project","p":32},{"i":39,"t":"You should see a startup message and no errors. If something fails, see Configuration.","s":"3. Check the output","u":"/docs/getting-started/quickstart","h":"#3-check-the-output","p":32},{"i":41,"t":"Follow the first tutorial Read the architecture overview","s":"Next steps","u":"/docs/getting-started/quickstart","h":"